<title>UK: Falklands awards oil licenses, Argentine bid fails.</title>
<headline>Falklands awards oil licenses, Argentine bid fails.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Falkland Islands government on Monday said it would issue licenses to 13 companies to explore for oil in waters to the north of the British territory.</p>
<p>Chief Executive of the Falklands Islands government Andrew Gurr said a joint application from British Gas and Argentina's Yacimientos Petroliferos Fiscales (YPF) was the only bid that failed.</p>
<p>&quot;That was the only consortium that got nothing but that was partly because they limited their bidding to the two most successful tranches,&quot; Gurr told Reuters.</p>
</text>
